			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Hello,
<br />

<br />
  This is TangleFoot a rather short and troublesome halfling druid on VS whom has been converted into a much taller if a lot bluer NE druid on Emerald Dream.
<br />

<br />
  I've been playing EQ for a number of years and had been playing my Druid mainly with AoT before joing up and changing over to my Cleric (Ophellia) with the DR merger.
<br />

<br />
  I stopped playing a few months ago about the time that WOW was released due to marital problems. I did start to play WOW and mess about because the time requirements to do this was much less than what was needed to do the major raids in EQ. My marital issues have been resolved via a divorce and now my playing time will be a bit higher and I'm looking to get back into the thick of things. Sadly, I've returned to VS to find that it's a hollow shell of it's former glory.
<br />

<br />
  TangleFoot is a level 32 NE Druid and Ophellia is  level 25 Human Priest. I know that I need to pick one and stay with it but so far I've not been too worried about it since I suspect that getting to level 60 is not that hard and that content is still a bit low and that lots of people will end up creating an alt or two (though I could be wrong).
<br />

<br />
  I've not worried about the build of either of them so far as I plan on respeccing them sometime in the near future. Right now Tangle is a Balance/Restoration build and Ophellia is mainly Shadow Specced.
<br />

<br />
  I've been playing WOW since it started and actually have 9 characters (one of each class including a Shaman) that are all level 24 or higher. This was mainly to learn how each class plays and to find the style that I was most comfortable with. I like them all but I find that oddly enough Druid and Priest are still best suited to me. Hmmm level 24 x 9 = 216 talk about leveling.
<br />

<br />
  Tangle is a Leatherworker/Skinner and Oph is a Alchemist/Herbalist both are reasonably well advanced for their level.
<br />

<br />
  Right now I'm still playing about during working hours (playing while getting paid) but can and will play evenings and weekends as needed.
<br />

<br />
  See you all around.<br />_________________<br />What do you mean where are we?</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
